{"t": 0.01, "kind": "session_inputs", "cell": "test_r2r_es_codex_gpt-5.5_default_oracle-none", "harness": "codex", "model": "gpt-5.5", "system_prompt": "You are controlling a robot in a real indoor environment (a photorealistic 3D scan of a building). You interact only through these tools:\n\n- observe(): look through the robot's forward-facing camera (returns an RGB image).\n- step(actions): execute movement actions in order. 0 = STOP (permanently ends the episode \u2014 declares you have reached the goal), 1 = move forward 0.25 m, 2 = turn left 15 degrees, 3 = turn right 15 degrees, 4 = tilt the camera up 30 degrees, 5 = tilt the camera down 30 degrees (tilt changes the camera pitch only, not your position or heading).\n\nYour task is to follow this navigation instruction to its endpoint:\n\n\"Walk forward, take a left around the corner and walk all the way to the end of the hallway, and stop at the door before the bedroom.\"\n\nRules:\n- Alternate observing and stepping: look, decide where the instruction wants you to go next, move, look again.\n- You have a budget of 500 movement actions.\n- You succeed only if you issue action 0 (STOP) while within 3 meters of the instruction's endpoint. STOP is permanent \u2014 issue it only when you believe you are at the goal.\n- Turning in place (e.g. step([2,2,2,2,2,2])) is a cheap way to look around when unsure.\n- Tilt changes persist until you change them again; level the camera again before moving on, and check your camera pitch before interpreting a view.\n- Work autonomously until you stop; nobody can answer questions.\n", "first_prompt": "Begin navigating. Call observe() first to see where you are.", "tool_schemas": [{"name": "observe", "description": "Look through the robot's forward-facing camera. Returns the current egocentric RGB view. Pure read \u2014 does not advance the simulator or consume step budget.", "input_schema": {"properties": {}, "title": "observeArguments", "type": "object"}}, {"name": "step", "description": "Execute a sequence of movement actions, in order.\n\nActions: 0 = STOP (permanently ENDS the episode \u2014 issue it only when you believe the robot is within 3 meters of the goal), 1 = move forward 0.25 m, 2 = turn left 15 degrees, 3 = turn right 15 degrees, 4 = tilt the camera up 30 degrees, 5 = tilt the camera down 30 degrees (tilt changes the camera pitch only, not your position or heading; pitch is clamped to \u00b160\u00b0).\n\nExecutes sequentially and halts early if the episode ends. Returns how many actions ran, total steps taken, remaining budget, and whether the episode is over. The camera view changes after stepping \u2014 call observe() to see the result.", "input_schema": {"properties": {"actions": {"items": {"type": "integer"}, "title": "Actions", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["actions"], "title": "stepArguments", "type": "object"}}], "effort": "medium", "options": {"argv": ["codex", "exec", "--json", "--skip-git-repo-check", "--sandbox", "read-only", "-c", "model = \"gpt-5.5\"", "-c", "model_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"", "-c", "model_reasoning_summary = \"detailed\"", "-c", "mcp_servers.env.command = \"/home/xukai/code/agentic-nav/MIP/envs/mip/bin/python\"", "-c", "mcp_servers.env.args = [\"/home/xukai/code/agentic-nav/MIP/exp_workspace/oracleES/mcp/bridge.py\"]", "-c", "mcp_servers.env.env = { BAREES_SERVER_URL = \"http://127.0.0.1:9200\", BAREES_TASK = \"nav\", BAREES_ACTIONS = \"6\", BAREES_STEP_BUDGET = \"500\", BAREES_TURN_BUDGET = \"0\", BAREES_BARE = \"1\", BAREES_AUTO_OBSERVE = \"0\", BAREES_LIVE_DIR = \"/home/xukai/code/agentic-nav/MIP/outputs/codex/test_r2r_es_codex_gpt-5.5_default_oracle-none/live_7\", BAREES_ORACLE = \"none\", BAREES_ORACLE_JSON = \"/home/xukai/code/agentic-nav/task3/oracle_by_index_rand100.json\", BAREES_ORACLE_MASK_FINAL = \"1\", BAREES_ORACLE_PARAMS = \"/home/xukai/code/agentic-nav/task3/rules_v0.json\", BAREES_EPISODE_INDEX = \"7\", EH_EXECUTOR = \"codex\" }", "-c", "mcp_servers.env.default_tools_appro